# Type:   (feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore, security)
# Scope:  (module name, component, or area affected)
# Issue:  (GitHub issue number, if applicable)
# Security: (security-related changes, if any)

# Example:
# feat(auth): add JWT token validation
# fix(database): resolve connection timeout issue
# docs(api): update authentication documentation
# security(crypto): fix timing attack vulnerability

# Commit message format:
# <type>(<scope>): <description>

# Description should:
# - Be written in imperative mood
# - Be concise but descriptive
# - Reference issue numbers if applicable
# - Include security impact if relevant

# Security-related commits should include:
# - Type: security
# - Detailed description of vulnerability
# - CVSS score if available
# - References to CVEs or advisories

# Example security commit:
# security(auth): fix SQL injection vulnerability
# Fixes SQL injection in user authentication endpoint
# CVSS: 9.8 - Critical
# References: CVE-2024-1234

# Before committing, ensure:
# - All tests pass
# - Security scans are clean
# - Documentation is updated
# - No secrets or credentials are exposed